            </note>
            <note corresp="#d258-f2" n="1" xml:id="d258-f2-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d251">Document 251</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d258-f3" n="2" xml:id="d258-f3-content">
                <p><ref target="#d254">Document 254</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d258-f4" n="3" xml:id="d258-f4-content">
                <p>As outlined in the introduction of the report the task of the study group under
                    Cary was to determine the most desirable force posture for the ROK for
                    1962-1970. The group was specifically enjoined to consider possible alternative
                    basic policies for the defense of Korea.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d258-f5" n="4" xml:id="d258-f5-content">
                <p>Printed from a copy that indicates McNamara signed the original.</p>
            </note>
